<article class="env-lemma" id="01I9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01I9">Lemma <span data-tag="01I9">26.7.3</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S), \mathcal{O}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)})$, $(Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y) = (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R), \mathcal{O}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)})$ be affine schemes. Let $\psi : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of affine schemes, corresponding to the ring map $\psi ^\sharp : R \to S$ (see Lemma <a href="/tag/01I2" data-tag="01I2">26.6.5</a>). </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We have $\psi ^* \widetilde M = \widetilde{S \otimes _ R M}$ functorially in the $R$-module $M$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We have $\psi _* \widetilde N = \widetilde{N_ R}$ functorially in the $S$-module $N$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first assertion follows from the identification in Lemma <a href="/tag/01I7" data-tag="01I7">26.7.1</a> and the result of Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01BJ" data-tag="01BJ">17.10.7</a>. The second assertion follows from the fact that $\psi ^{-1}(D(f)) = D(\psi ^\sharp (f))$ and hence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \psi _* \widetilde N(D(f)) = \widetilde N(D(\psi ^\sharp (f))) = N_{\psi ^\sharp (f)} = (N_ R)_ f = \widetilde{N_ R}(D(f))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>